#: ../drivers/radtel_rt880g.py:2562
msgid "Turns APRS on or off. With APRS on, the radio sends its own APRS data to other stations and decodes the APRS data it receives. When received data contains a position, the radio shows the direction and distance to that station."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/radtel_rt880g.py:2420
msgid "Turns background GPS reception on or off."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/radtel_rt880g.py:1308
msgid "Turns monitoring of the NOAA weather channels on or off."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/radtel_rt880g.py:1277
msgid "Turns noise reduction of the transmitted audio on or off. The manual lists only Off and On and does not explain the 840-1000MHz choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1083
msgid "Turns on Bluetooth so that the radio can be programmed wirelessly from a phone app."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/radtel_rt880g.py:2846 ../drivers/radtel_rt880g.py:2866
#, python-format
msgid "Turns on digipeater %d. When the path in received APRS data matches Digipeater %d Name, the radio forwards the data."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/radtel_rt880g.py:2769
msgid "Turns on queue beaconing, with the interval set by Queue Interval. The manual names this mode without explaining it."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1338
msgid "Turns on split frequency operation: the radio receives on VFO-A and transmits on VFO-B, or the other way round. The two VFOs may use different modes and even different bands."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:976
msgid "Turns on the DSP contour filter, which gently cuts or boosts one part of the receive passband. Cutting suppresses interference or excessive components of a signal, boosting brings out the components that make it easier to understand."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1045
msgid "Turns on the DSP digital noise reduction, which reduces random background noise on the HF and 50 MHz bands. It is especially effective on SSB."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1687
msgid "Turns on the IF noise blanker, which reduces short pulses of noise such as those from vehicle ignition systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1010
msgid "Turns on the IF notch filter, a narrow and deep filter that removes a single interfering carrier or whistle from inside the receive passband."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1717
msgid "Turns on the built-in electronic CW keyer, for a keyer paddle plugged into the KEY jack. Turn it off to use a straight key or an external keyer."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1619
msgid "Turns on the privacy function the manual calls Encryption for this channel. Other radios can only understand the conversation if they have it turned on as well and use the same DCS code."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/radtel_rt880g.py:1971
msgid "Turns on the temporary receive thresholds, which the manual calls Temporary Receive Threshold Open. While it is on, RSSI Threshold and Noise Threshold set how easily a signal opens the receiver."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/radtel_rt880g.py:2008
msgid "Turns on the temporary transmit power values, which the manual calls Temporary Power Open. While it is on, the power value of each frequency range sets the transmit power."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/radtel_rt880g.py:1680
msgid "Turns side key 1 and side key 2 into extra PTT keys: side key 1 transmits on area B and side key 2 on area C. The functions assigned to the two keys are then disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/radtel_rt880g.py:1132
